.TH wsblast 1  "wsblast 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
wsblast \- High\-performance WebSocket load\-testing CLI with percentile latency & CI gating
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwsblast\fR [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-connections\fR] [\fB\-\-ramp\-rate\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-requests\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-payload\fR] [\fB\-\-payload\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-binary\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-header\fR] [\fB\-\-subprotocol\fR] [\fB\-\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-message\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-match\fR] [\fB\-\-ping\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-p50\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-p95\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-p99\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-p999\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-error\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-throughput\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-header\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-apikey\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-apikey\-header\fR] [\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-operation\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-operation\fR] [\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-variables\fR] [\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-extensions\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-compare\fR] [\fB\-\-compare\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-regression\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-reconnect\fR] [\fB\-\-scenario\fR] [\fB\-\-phase\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIURL\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
wsblast stresses WebSocket targets, computes high\-resolution latency percentiles (p50/p95/p99/p99.9), maps failure taxonomy, and gates CI pipelines via SLO thresholds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Target WebSocket endpoint flag (alternative to positional argument)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-connections\fR \fI<NUM>\fR [default: 50]
Number of concurrent WebSocket connection workers
.TP
\fB\-\-ramp\-rate\fR \fI<WORKERS_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 0]
Connection ramp rate in workers per second (0 = spawn all connections immediately)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 10s]
Total test duration including the connection ramp (e.g., \*(Aq10s\*(Aq, \*(Aq30s\*(Aq, \*(Aq2m\*(Aq, \*(Aq500ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-requests\fR \fI<NUM>\fR
Maximum total messages to send across all workers (optional limit)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<MSG_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 0]
Message rate per connection per second (0 = unthrottled / maximum possible)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-payload\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Inline message payload to send (supports {{timestamp}}, {{worker_id}}, {{seq}})
.TP
\fB\-\-payload\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Path to a file containing the message payload
.TP
\fB\-\-binary\fR
Send payload as WebSocket binary frames instead of text frames
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-header\fR \fI<HEADER:VALUE>\fR
Custom HTTP header to include in the WebSocket handshake (can be specified multiple times)
.TP
\fB\-\-subprotocol\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Optional WebSocket subprotocol to request during handshake
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: echo]
Load testing execution mode
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
echo: Send request frame, await response, and record round\-trip latency (RTT)
.IP \(bu 2
stream: Continuously stream frames without awaiting per\-frame acknowledgments
.IP \(bu 2
listen: Connect workers and passively record incoming server\-pushed broadcast messages
.IP \(bu 2
graphql\-ws: Apollo GraphQL WS protocol (subscriptions)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 5s]
Connection handshake timeout (e.g., \*(Aq5s\*(Aq, \*(Aq2000ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-message\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 5s]
Per\-message response timeout in echo mode (e.g., \*(Aq5s\*(Aq, \*(Aq1000ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-match\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: first]
Echo reply matching: first (default: the first data frame after a send is the reply), exact, or json:POINTER (an RFC 6901 pointer such as json:/seq)

first: the first text or binary frame received after a send is taken as the reply, even when it is an unrelated server push such as a broadcast or heartbeat, which then records a wrong RTT.

exact: the reply must be byte\-identical to the frame that was sent.

json:POINTER: the reply is parsed as JSON and the value at the RFC 6901 pointer (e.g. json:/seq) must equal this request\*(Aqs {{seq}}, as a number or a numeric string. The payload must contain {{seq}}.

With exact and json:POINTER, other data frames are counted as unsolicited and the worker keeps waiting for its reply until \-\-message\-timeout.
.TP
\fB\-\-ping\-interval\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 0s]
Periodic ping heartbeat interval (e.g., \*(Aq10s\*(Aq, \*(Aq0s\*(Aq to disable)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-p50\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
SLO threshold: Maximum acceptable p50 round\-trip latency (e.g., \*(Aq10ms\*(Aq, \*(Aq500us\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-p95\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
SLO threshold: Maximum acceptable p95 round\-trip latency (e.g., \*(Aq50ms\*(Aq, \*(Aq20ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-p99\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
SLO threshold: Maximum acceptable p99 round\-trip latency (e.g., \*(Aq100ms\*(Aq, \*(Aq50ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-p999\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
SLO threshold: Maximum acceptable p99.9 round\-trip latency (e.g., \*(Aq250ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-error\-rate\fR \fI<FLOAT>\fR
SLO threshold: Maximum acceptable error rate fraction (e.g., \*(Aq0.01\*(Aq for 1%, \*(Aq0.001\*(Aq for 0.1%)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-throughput\fR \fI<RPS>\fR
SLO threshold: Minimum required message throughput (messages/sec)
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-type\fR \fI<TYPE>\fR [default: none]
Authentication type (none, static, apikey)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
none: No authentication
.IP \(bu 2
static: Static bearer token
.IP \(bu 2
apikey: API Key
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Static token for auth (used with \-\-auth\-type static)
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-header\fR \fI<HEADER>\fR [default: Authorization]
Header name for static token (used with \-\-auth\-type static)
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-apikey\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
API Key (used with \-\-auth\-type apikey)
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-apikey\-header\fR \fI<HEADER>\fR [default: X\-API\-Key]
API Key header name (used with \-\-auth\-type apikey)
.TP
\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-operation\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
GraphQL WS operation name
.TP
\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-operation\fR \fI<OPERATION>\fR
GraphQL WS operation (query/mutation/subscription)
.TP
\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-variables\fR \fI<JSON>\fR
GraphQL WS variables (JSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-graphql\-ws\-extensions\fR \fI<JSON>\fR
GraphQL WS extensions (JSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output report format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: Human\-readable styled terminal tables
.IP \(bu 2
json: Schema\-versioned JSON for CI parsing and metric archiving
.IP \(bu 2
markdown: GitHub Flavored Markdown table for PR comments and job summaries
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\fR \fI<FILE>...\fR
Compare two JSON reports for regression detection
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\-threshold\fR \fI<PERCENT>\fR [default: 10]
Regression threshold percentage (default: 10%)
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-regression\fR
Fail on regression (exit code 2)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write output report to the specified file path
.TP
\fB\-\-tui\fR
Launch interactive terminal dashboard (TUI)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Suppress interactive progress bar (recommended for non\-interactive CI/CD runners)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-reconnect\fR
End a connection\*(Aqs worker after a timeout, I/O error or server close instead of reconnecting with backoff
.TP
\fB\-\-scenario\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Path to scenario YAML file defining multi\-phase test (conflicts with individual flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-phase\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Run only a specific phase from the scenario by name
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIURL\fR]
Target WebSocket URL (e.g., ws://127.0.0.1:9001/ws or wss://api.example.com/stream)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
